cd2226505eee8d91a1cdffc7e3f8c96ed63cf602c5ed1a8f6","file":"preprints/A-PD4-group-without-an-aspherical-manifold-model-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex","line":94,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"2f635fede761e14178fed2c2304182dabb7e97341948dfa02aef4ffab2eaae50","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-PD4-group-without-an-aspherical-manifold-model-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:cb45f57396f8ae2cd2226505eee8d91a1cdffc7e3f8c96ed63cf602c5ed1a8f6","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-PD4-group-without-an-aspherical-manifold-model-September-24-2026/build/paper.tex#L94"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is a finitely presented group $G$ with a finite, oriented,\nfour-dimensional aspherical Poincar\\'e complex $Q$ such that\n\\[\n H^i(G;\\Z G)=0\\quad(i\\ne4),\\qquad H^4(G;\\Z G)\\cong\\Z\n\\]\nwith trivial right $G$-action on the last group, but no closed aspherical\ntopological four-manifold has fundamental group $G$.\nIn particular the trivial left $\\Z G$-module $\\Z$ has a finite resolution\nby finitely generated free modules."}
